{"id": "xsierra", "name": "Gola Rainforest National Park", "short": "Gola Rainforest", "place": "Sierra Leone", "lat": 7.6, "lon": -11.1, "side": "r", "cont": "Africa", "country": "Sierra Leone", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Upper Guinea rainforest where chimps, pygmy hippos and crowned eagles share the canopy.", "tip": {"id": "ficus", "title": "Fell the fig trees", "text": "Figs feed elephants, monkeys, hornbills and chimpanzees. Set Fig trees to -100% and watch fruit-eaters drop, then the monkeys, chimps and eagles that depend on them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Gola Rainforest National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gola_Rainforest_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Pygmy hippopotamus", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pygmy_hippopotamus"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Western chimpanzee", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_chimpanzee"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: African forest elephant", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_forest_elephant"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Crowned eagle", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowned_eagle"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Leopard", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopard"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Gola Rainforest National Park", "icon": "elephant", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "Light reaching the canopy drives the forest; very little of it penetrates to the dim understorey."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "heavy rainfall", "xh": 0.37, "desc": "The forest sits in a very wet part of West Africa, and the rains keep its streams, swamps and soils moist."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil and leaf litter", "xh": 0.62, "desc": "Fallen leaves, fruit and wood rot into a thin nutrient layer that the trees and ferns draw on."}, {"id": "stream", "sp": "streams and swamps", "xh": 0.84}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.94, "desc": "Break down dead leaves, wood, dung and carcasses in the warm, damp forest, returning nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "ficus", "sp": "ficus", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Figs fruit through much of the year in tropical forests, which makes them a dependable food for many monkeys, birds and mammals.", "ic": "aspen"}, {"id": "oilpalm", "sp": "elaeis guineensis", "xh": 0.33, "name": "African oil palm", "desc": "A West African palm whose oily fruits are eaten by chimpanzees, elephants and rodents.", "ic": "sage"}, {"id": "plagio", "sp": "plagiosiphon emarginatus", "xh": 0.57}, {"id": "fern", "sp": "dicranopteris linearis", "xh": 0.82}, {"id": "elephant", "sp": "loxodonta cyclotis", "xh": 0.05, "desc": "A forest-dwelling elephant that eats bark, leaves and many fruits, and spreads seeds over long distances. Its population in Gola has dwindled."}, {"id": "hippo", "sp": "choeropsis liberiensis", "xh": 0.18, "desc": "A shy nocturnal hippo that hides in rivers by day and forages at dusk on herbs, ferns and fallen fruit. Gola is one of its refuges."}, {"id": "redcol", "sp": "piliocolobus badius", "xh": 0.31, "desc": "A leaf-eating monkey of the forest canopy, recorded eating Plagiosiphon. It is prey for chimpanzees and crowned eagles."}, {"id": "olivecol", "sp": "procolobus verus", "xh": 0.44}, {"id": "diana", "sp": "cercopithecus diana", "xh": 0.57, "desc": "A canopy guenon that eats fruit and insects. It is hunted by chimpanzees, leopards and crowned eagles."}, {"id": "hornbill", "sp": "ceratogymna elata", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "gamrat", "sp": "cricetomys gambianus", "xh": 0.83}, {"id": "royal", "sp": "neotragus pygmaeus", "xh": 0.95}, {"id": "chimp", "sp": "pan troglodytes verus", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "An omnivore that eats fruit and hunts monkeys. Gola holds a population of over 300.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "hawk", "s